## Frequently asked questions

### Is an Amazon listing audit worth it compared with other spend?

Yes when weak listing copy is the problem. No when price, stock or review count is the problem. The audit checks keyword gaps, indexing, titles, bullets, images and A+ Content on your top 5 ASINs. A fixed £495 audit is a one-off cost where PPC is a running cost. Better copy does not fix a price, stock or review problem. I will say so. The free 20-minute diagnosis tells you which case you are in. I do not promise a ranking or sales result.

### What happens to reviews when SKU changes create new ASINs?

Reviews belong to the ASIN. A new ASIN starts without them. In the audit I check three things. First: can the old and new listings be linked as variations or merged where Amazon allows it for your category? Second: does the new listing keep the keyword coverage of the old one? Third: is the old listing still live, suppressed or competing with the new one? What Amazon permits depends on your category and account. I confirm the options after seeing the listings.

### Do you rewrite the listings or do I?

Either. I can rewrite your listings at £175 per ASIN or your team can work from the audit. Some clients have me rewrite all listing copy, backend terms and A+ briefs. Others take the audit and recommendations back to their in-house team. I stay available for questions.

### Do you work with Amazon UK sellers only?

No. I work with sellers on Amazon.co.uk and Amazon.com. I am based in Reading in Berkshire and work online with sellers across the UK and with brands selling on Amazon.com.

### What is the difference between an Amazon SEO consultant and an Amazon agency?

An Amazon SEO consultant is one specialist who does the work personally. An agency typically assigns an account team and often bundles PPC management. My Amazon SEO consultancy is one person: me. I do not manage PPC. I focus on organic listing performance. Comparing the best Amazon SEO agencies for UK sellers in 2026? Ask who will do the work and whether PPC is bundled into the fee.

